{"key":"AiDesignerWindow","text":"## AiDesignerWindow\n\nThe **AI Designer** is where you design an AI system as a picture: place\n**Data**, **Model** and **Algorithm** boxes, wire what feeds what, and send the\nwhole design to the xmlIT service with one click. The reply comes back as a\nnode on the same canvas, and any single operation can be tried against the\ngorpIT math service before you commit.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.50, 0.03 | The gear menu holds New, Open Saved, Open Starter Sample, Import (including Import SAI XML), Layout and Convert. The two code buttons open the XML panel and the well-formedness validator; the map button toggles the minimap. Right-click for Save to GitHub, Export, Undo and Redo.\nRun Bar | 0.50, 0.09 | Run posts the design to xmlIT. Check validates it locally without touching the network. The xmlIT label shows the endpoint; click to edit it, clear it to go back to the Magic Portal. The dropdown on the right switches between the Class, Sequence, Activity and State Machine views.\nConstructs | 0.04, 0.50 | Click Data, Model or Algorithm to drop a new box at the center of the view with starter rows.\nCanvas | 0.45, 0.50 | The design. Drag boxes to move them; the colored lines are derived from the wiring and redraw themselves. Right-click a box to change its construct, add Input or Output ports on an algorithm, or Set Model on a data box.\nXML Panel | 0.85, 0.50 | The saved document in Tree or Raw form, and a read-only Wire tab showing the exact bytes Run sends.\n\n---\n\n### The three constructs\n\n- **Data** — rows of real values. A data box is *of* a model: right-click it and choose *Set Model* to say which\n- **Model** — the shape of the data: named variables with types and units, and the operations that act on them\n- **Algorithm** — the work. It declares one **Input** model and one **Output** model, its operations, and the flow of expressions that runs them\n\nRight-click any box and use *Change Construct* to turn it into another kind.\n\n### Wiring\n\n- **Input / Output** — right-click an algorithm to choose which model feeds it and which model it fills. These are the only connections you draw; they are saved with the design\n- **Reference** — right-click a variable row and choose *Set Reference* to point it at another model. The reference line is drawn from that row\n- **Instance** — a data box's model draws its own line; you never create it by hand\n- **Compose** — when an algorithm has more than one input, right-click it and choose *Compose inputs into one model*; the designer builds a model of references so the algorithm still has exactly one input\n- Colored lines are derived and redraw on every change. Right-click one to read why it exists\n\n### Running and checking\n\n- **Run** — sends the design and its current values to xmlIT. The result appears as a **Returned** node on the canvas, read-only and never saved with the design\n- **Check** — lists Errors, Warnings and Info in an overlay. Click a finding to jump to its box. The scope line says how many units and collapse policies were checked. Click Check again to close it\n- **Test…** — right-click an operation row to open the Test panel: fill in the values, set an expected result, and *Run test* sends just that expression to gorpIT\n- On the web the endpoint must stay the Magic Portal; a direct address works only in the Unity Editor\n\n### Views\n\n- **Class Diagram** — the boxes and wiring; the only view where you edit\n- **Sequence Diagram** — the calls implied by the Input and Output wiring, in declared order\n- **Activity Diagram** — the values flowing into each algorithm, its operations, and what comes out, each annotated with its unit\n- **State Machine** — a pane under the canvas showing the selected construct's flow as states and guarded transitions. Right-click in the pane to author states and transitions. The step bar walks the flow one transition at a time using the values you type in\n\n### Files\n\n- Saves as an .xml document in Files/AiDesign under your account; the default name is *AI Design*\n- **Import SAI XML** loads a Gestalt or SAI file from the bundled samples and replaces the whole diagram (it asks first when the canvas is not empty)\n- **Open Starter Sample** loads a small worked design to explore\n- The XML panel's **Wire** tab is exactly what Run sends: an xaiml envelope around the saved document plus the input values\n\n### Shortcuts\n\nAll shortcuts are shared with the UML Window and pause while you are typing in a field or while the Test or Check panel is open.\n\n- **Ctrl/Cmd+Z** undo, **Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+Z** or **Ctrl/Cmd+Y** redo\n- **Ctrl/Cmd+A / C / X / V / D** — select all, copy, cut, paste, duplicate\n- **Delete / Backspace** — delete the selected boxes\n- **Tab / Shift+Tab** — cycle through boxes; **Esc** clears the selection\n\n### Status: Beta\n### Purpose: AIDesign\n\n---","screenshot":""}